# What `docker build` must not send to the daemon.
#
# Both images are built with the repository root as their context, so without this file the
# daemon receives `node_modules/` (a gigabyte of it, hard-linked by Bun), `services/toolbox/.venv`
# and `.local/` — the music library itself. That was measured during P02-verify-1 and carried as
# technical debt until P10.
#
# The rule of thumb: everything here is either regenerated inside the image (`bun install`,
# `uv sync`, `bun run build`) or has no business in one (state, secrets, reports, tests fixtures
# that only the host runs).

# --- installed and built artefacts, all regenerated in the image -------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.output/
**/.output/
.nitro/
**/.nitro/
dist/
**/dist/
.vite/
**/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- mutable state; `.local/` is the music library and Navidrome's database ---
.local/
**/.local/
*.log

# --- secrets. They arrive as environment variables, never in a layer ---------
.env
.env.*
!.env.production.example
!.env.example

# --- version control and editor ----------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- host-only: browser tests, their artefacts, and generated route trees -----
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
apps/web/e2e/
apps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts

# --- documentation and agent scaffolding -------------------------------------
*.md
!services/toolbox/README.md
docker-compose*.yml
